+EXACT FOUR PRIMITIVE RUNNER — INACTIVE UNTIL FRESH ROOT ADMISSION
+
+No compiler/native/service execution is performed by preparation or tests.
+Current storage live07 failed; this package does NOT authorize a retry or launch.
+Mount-repair08 owns the separate storage fixture work. Root must review successful
+future storage qualification and issue fresh owner/grants before using drive.
+No application eligibility review, scene/compose retry, compiler/library edit,
+D267 allocator, D289 typedArena/fixedspread, A333 compiler-body or rejected variant.
+
+SOURCE CONTRACT
+runner.py binds the exact accepted plan.json SHA256
+1d2bf57861fdc0e9d8f5e1f4410ee6cb6ace99273cc706fc93090db43dcdd976.
+Order: int64 (9 assertions), extraction (11), unicode (16), then the original
+native_named_syntax_dependency (2). First three copy the COMPLETE unchanged
+4361-byte test_json_binary64.vkf; fourth has no dependency. No source rewriting
+by this materializer. Normalization is the separately pinned existing tool.
+No native47/original419, renderer, ordered-reader, metadata/reference or API
+credit follows automatically, even from later successful primitive execution.
+
+EXECUTABLE INTERFACES (paths below are parameters, not issued authority)
+After root applies the patch, from the repository:
+  python3 -B integration/0.7.4/native-primitive-runner/test_runner.py \
+    --repo "$PWD" --artifacts /ABSOLUTE/NEW/ISOLATED/TEST-DIRECTORY
+The test fixture never selects real compiler/controller operations. It uses real
+input hashes and byte copies, short Python scripts, <=0.12s deadline cases and
+2s emergency fixture sleeps, with every direct/descendant child killed and waited.
+Tests retain raw evidence in their explicit artifact directory. Do not select an
+operational attempt directory for tests. fake_tool.py is not used by the CLI.
+
+Root prepares ONE request using request.template.json, fills every null, and pins
+it outside all enrolled writable roots. No issued config or owner-state writer is
+provided here. request contains:
+- Fresh owner, A/F lane, positive iteration, unique attempt and CURRENT integrated
+  source_commit. attempt_root must be canonical policy.root.path/attempt and ABSENT.
+- Fresh installed controller/helpers/config/policy/transition/owned-helper/ledger
+  pins, copied from ROOT REVIEWED authority, never an old worker's grant.
+- live_qualification_review pin: a root-written JSON with coordinator equal to the
+  sole coordinator and BOTH storage_v4_qualified and native_primitives_authorized
+  true. The actual successful qualification receipts should be pinned in that
+  review and extra_inputs. A boolean is an explicit root decision, not a signature
+  or an independent technical proof. This task ships no such approval.
+- phase_bytes >=1073741824. This lower bound retains the provisional old estimate;
+  it is neither proof of capacity nor measured demand. v4 must actually admit it.
+- ram_peak_bytes exactly3221225472, or8589934592 for A only. No RAM changes here.
+  Root must establish the existing reviewed profile; A8 requires active7GiB high.
+  V4 restores A high to3GiB only after terminal join, as before.
+- timeout_seconds120..180, enclosing three30s children plus cleanup/controller time.
+- host_namespaces: exact readlinks /proc/self/ns/{pid,net} from the host at admission.
+- extra_inputs: additional exact root-reviewed OS/tool/runtime dependencies (e.g.
+  interpreter modules, systemd-run/bwrap/systemctl/busctl/git and their libraries).
+  Existing plan tool/runtime/stdlib pins and runner/request/spec are auto-included.
+  This is not a hermetic snapshot of every dynamically loaded OS library.
+- previous: pins of ALL earlier immutable bundle.json files, in exact accepted
+  order. First entry [], second[int64], third[int64,extraction], fourth adds unicode.
+  Earlier services must remain independently inspectable; failed or missing
+  predecessor evidence stops before the next controller is loaded/launched.
+
+  python3 -B integration/0.7.4/native-primitive-runner/runner.py prepare \
+    --request /ABSOLUTE/ROOT-REVIEWED/request.json \
+    --output /ABSOLUTE/NEW/FINAL-REVIEW-DIRECTORY
+
+Preparation reads hashes, generates a deterministic spec.json plus per-entry
+v4 grant.json, manifest.json and bundle.json. It creates ONLY the new final review
+directory, never the attempt, ledger, config, owners, services or budgets. It
+requires the root qualification review. Review artifacts have no launch authority
+until root separately pins/binds them in current v4 owners and capacity authority.
+Do not move or edit generated files: paths/hashes are part of the contract. Source
+changes require regeneration before admission. A failed prep directory is retained.
+
+Root reviews all artifacts and binds the exact fresh grant in owners-v4.json using
+its existing authorized mechanism. Owner transitions stay root-owned. No historical
+cap reset/refund, same failed attempt replay or old live qualification grant reuse.
+Then, and ONLY under fresh launch authority:
+  python3 -B integration/0.7.4/native-primitive-runner/runner.py drive \
+    --bundle /ABSOLUTE/FINAL-REVIEW-DIRECTORY/bundle.json --sha256 EXACT_BUNDLE_HASH
+
+Drive is one sequential step per invocation. It authenticates every prior success
+via the INSTALLED v4 Ledger and Controller.verify_join, including terminal systemd
+properties, original invocation/cgroup and pinned service-join receipt. It does
+not trust a summary passed=true alone. It validates exact request/spec/grant/
+manifest binding, creates an exclusive EMPTY attempt directory (required by v4),
+then calls installed Controller.current/outer. V4 alone reserves/charges/guards,
+launches the transient service and bwrap, and authenticates terminal service join.
+The driver performs no owner/config writes and does not install or modify v4.
+Controller.outer returns the actual payload result. A nonzero result or exception
+stops immediately. No automatic refill/retry/next launch. A pre-admission failure
+retains the empty path; it must not be reused. Root must review before new authority.
+After successful drive exits, root rebinds the next fresh grant and invokes drive
+for that entry. This deliberate boundary permits fresh per-entry authority and
+review without having a payload mutate its own owner state or issue later grants.
+
+EXACT CHILD CONTRACT / OUTPUTS
+For each admitted root R:
+  R/cwd/primitive/raw/<original entry basename + full dependency basenames>
+  R/cwd/primitive/normalized/source/<same basenames>
+  R/cwd/primitive/normalized/normalization.json
+  R/cwd/primitive/compiler/self_hosted/stdlib/... (all30 exact pinned files)
+  R/cwd/primitive/case.exe                  (must be absent before compilation)
+  R/cwd/primitive/home                     (private HOME)
+  R/cwd/primitive/stdin                    (empty; exact plan SHA)
+  R/cwd/primitive/{normalize,compile,run}.{stdout,stderr,json}
+  R/cwd/primitive/{materialization,result}.json
+  R/{tmpdir,cache,ccache,receipts}           (all charged, no outside spill)
+V4 also writes its existing admission/outer/stdout/stderr/service-join receipts
+under R/receipts. Every failure artifact stays charged and retained.
+
+The spec enumerates absolute argv, cwd, destinations, inputs, environment and
+expected runtime output. Normalize invokes the pinned Python interpreter's
+canonical regular-file target, -B, the unchanged normalize_module_aliases.py,
+--source-dir R/cwd/primitive/raw --output-dir R/cwd/primitive/normalized.
+Compile uses the exact D288 vkf-strict -b NORMALIZED_ENTRY -o R/.../case.exe
+--diagnostics. Run executes ONLY that newly produced regular executable, pinned
+before/after. Expected exit0, stdout/stderr empty. Compile diagnostics are retained;
+the accepted plan defines no exact compiler diagnostic text contract. Normalizer
+JSON, report hashes, exact closure and empty stderr are verified before compiling.
+
+V4 compatibility: storage_paths.pinned uses O_NOFOLLOW and allocated rejects all
+symlinks. Thus /usr/bin/python3 is authenticated against the original plan pin but
+executed/presented to v4 by its canonical regular-file path. Original tool/source
+pins remain in the spec. Historical native-gates stdlib symlinks are replaced with
+byte-identical regular copies (614150 source bytes total), preserving every full
+dependency. VKF_HOME still names the pinned read-only original toolchain. No v4
+policy relaxation, link accounting bypass, dependency stripping or source change.
+
+Child environment is an allowlist, not inherited caller variables:
+PATH=/home/viktor/.local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
+VKF_HOME and LD_LIBRARY_PATH exactly as plan.json (D288/B318 pinned toolchain)
+PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1; LC_ALL=C; LANG=C
+HOME=R/cwd/primitive/home; TMPDIR=TMP=TEMP=R/tmpdir
+XDG_CACHE_HOME=R/cache; CCACHE_DIR=R/ccache
+LD_PRELOAD,VKF_AST_CACHE,DISPLAY,WAYLAND_DISPLAY absent (other unlisted vars absent).
+No native/normalizer/compiler call occurs during preparation, fixture tests or
+source review. The payload CLI refuses the recorded host PID/net namespaces;
+that accident guard does not replace v4 admission/custody authentication.
+
+Each child gets <=30s measured monotonic deadline and file-backed stdin/out/err.
+The synchronous runner becomes a Linux subreaper, tracks PID/starttime ancestry
+and adopted detached descendants, terminates leftovers, reaps and records all
+joins. Any timeout, spawn failure, nonzero, orphan left by leader, unjoined child,
+input/output hash drift or unexpected runtime output stops. No parallel child
+execution. V4 KillMode=control-group and unshared PID namespace remain outer
+containment, particularly for crash/interruption outside Python's cleanup path.
+No kernel-quota, power-loss or adversarial same-UID guarantees are newly claimed.
+
+PROVISIONAL INCLUSIVE ACCOUNTING — NEVER A BUDGET GRANT
+Exactly1GiB per entry,4GiB cumulatively for four; no failure refund:
+  raw/normalized snapshots+metadata        8MiB
+  compiler temporaries+diagnostics       512MiB
+  executable+link outputs                128MiB
+  private tmp/home/cache                  64MiB
+  logs/receipts/joins                     16MiB
+  allocated-block slack+uncertainty      296MiB
+The regular stdlib copies are included in snapshots. The full estimate must be
+revalidated/admitted after future live qualification. Actual demand is unknown.
+F355's512MiB estimate retained927752192bytes; F359 retained about429MB. Tiny
+source files are not a native storage-cost measurement. Preserve permanent old
+charges, additive capacity policy, physical floors and existing RAM/cgroup guards.
